{
  "id": "22169_kitakusuru",
  "headword": "{帰宅|きたく}する",
  "reading": "きたくする",
  "romaji": "kitakusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb (intransitive)",
  "gloss": "to return home; to come home; to go home",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to return home; to come home; to go home",
      "explanation": "To go back to one's home, especially after work, school, or going out. Refers specifically to returning to one's own residence."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22169_kitakusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{夕方|ゆうがた}に{帰宅|きたく}した。",
      "english": "I came home in the evening.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22169_kitakusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{父|ちち}はいつも{遅|おそ}くに{帰宅|きたく}する。",
      "english": "My father always comes home late.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22169_kitakusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{仕事|しごと}が{終|お}わったら、まっすぐ{帰宅|きたく}するつもりです。",
      "english": "Once work is over, I plan to go straight home.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers specifically to returning to one's own home or residence, as opposed to simply going back somewhere. More formal and precise than {帰|かえ}る.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {帰宅|きたく}{時間|じかん} — time of returning home\n- {帰宅|きたく}{途中|とちゅう} — on the way home\n- {帰宅|きたく}{後|ご} — after returning home\n- {帰宅|きたく}が{遅|おそ}い — to come home late\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {帰|かえ}る — the general everyday word for going home; less formal\n- {帰還|きかん}する — to return (from far away, e.g., from overseas or war); literary\n- {帰省|きせい}する — to return to one's hometown or parents' home",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
